#only("1")[#voiceover("Behavioral Finance has introduced several key concepts that help explain financial behavior.")]
#only("2")[#voiceover("One is the idea of heuristics. These are the mental shortcuts or rules of thumb that we use to make decisions, which can sometimes lead to biases or errors in judgment.")]
#only("3")[#voiceover("Another is Prospect Theory, which looks at how people make decisions when there's risk involved. It suggests that people don't always make purely rational choices based on expected outcomes.")]
#only("4")[#voiceover("Behavioral Finance also studies market anomalies. These are events in financial markets that seem to contradict traditional theories, like the Efficient Market Hypothesis. Behavioral Finance offers alternative explanations based on psychological factors.")]

